Experiment No.: 7

Title

Interfacing 7-Segment Display with Arduino

Aim

To interface a 7-segment display with Arduino.

Theory

A 7-segment display consists of seven LEDs arranged to display numerical digits. Arduino controls each segment using digital output pins.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
7-Segment Display
Resistors
Jumper Wires
Procedure
Connect 7-segment display pins to Arduino.
Configure Arduino pins as outputs.
Upload the display program.
Observe the displayed digit.
Code
int segPins[7]={2,3,4,5,6,7,8};

byte digit0[7]={1,1,1,1,1,1,0};

void setup()
{
  for(int i=0;i<7;i++)
    pinMode(segPins[i],OUTPUT);
}

void loop()
{
  for(int i=0;i<7;i++)
    digitalWrite(segPins[i],digit0[i]);

  delay(1000);
}
Output

Digit 0 is displayed on the 7-segment display.

Result

The 7-segment display was successfully interfaced with Arduino.

Conclusion

The operation of a 7-segment display using Arduino was studied.
